Provenance

Workflow skills for Australian public-practice and contracting-business
accounting, written independently, from scratch, in my own time and on my own
equipment.


The v0.3.0 development expansion uses OpenAccountants Australian topic names
for gap identification. No OpenAccountants Guide bodies were copied or
adapted. The new workflow text is original; primary-source starting points
and their retrieval limitations are recorded beside each skill.

Additional intake and handoff gaps were identified by reviewing TaxMate
Australia (nijanthan-dev/taxmate-australia), tree
42ba67d458439e7882a3e8e0d76bfa6efdecbad7, on 6 October 2026. The new workflow
text is independently written for these skills. TaxMate runtime code,
generated source text, cached ATO material and tax tables were not copied.
The comparison and source licence are recorded in docs/taxmate-adoptions.md.

Additional workflow and regression patterns were inspected on 6 October 2026
in these MIT-licensed software repositories:

- hearthresearch/citefact, 469bb993e4047b5f3679877bdd4c710485e4e316
- marinasofia/statement-agent, b34c2ddc3062eff247e151d26fb126241162cab4
- kiwizznz/au-tax-return, 00256983631cc88cf6f08d78166351ac6d5174d5
- cynco-labs/ai-accounting-skills, 8d527e57164ee6581612178670234778b0a29440
- gunba/australian-legal-mcp, f900398e92d509031402534eac1803b45f376a21
- FoundrySoftHQ/agent-for-accounting, 7a9e8f9a81eb314b70418051b75213cf6230a01f

The new instructions and fabricated validation cards are independently
written. No upstream code, guide bodies, corpus text, rate tables, email
access or hosted-service integration is imported.

The short-stay accommodation topic gap, the contract-date CGT timing card and
a test against hard-coded figures in skill prose were identified on
15 October 2026 by reviewing the MIT-licensed darrentmorgan/au-accounting,
commit 8576474dbe0c. The au-short-stay-accommodation workflow and its cards
are independently written from ATO, legislation and State Revenue Office
Victoria sources read that day, and tests/test_skill_figures.py is
independently written. No upstream skill text,
evaluation case, code, rates data or refusal codes were copied.

The idea of a pre-lodgement review list came from the published feature list
of william-laverty/ato-mcp (AGPL-3.0), commit aa0d341bbca4, on 15 October
2026. The au-pre-lodgement-review workflow is an original design written
from ATO sources; no ato-mcp code, schemas, prompts or prose were used.

The idea of a reconciliation break-trace workflow, with a one-sentence cause
per break and a diagnose-only boundary, came from the break-trace skill in
the Apache-2.0-licensed anthropics/financial-services, commit
574ed3624aeb, read on 20 October 2026. The reconciliation-break-trace
workflow and its cards are independently written for Australian practice
ledgers; no upstream skill text, prompts, schemas or code were copied.
